      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "We agreed to go with dollar solar back in march 2017. I asked weekly for updates of when installation and delivery of solar would be. Initially Tom was enthusiastic and interested. Months passed with weekly calls to say installation ' would be next week'. We referred friends to get a quote from dollar solar, and next thing Tom was engaging with us again and installation would be ' 'next week'. Our friends decided not to go with dollar solar and then installation didn't occur. Continued to call Tom, who often didn't answer and then when he did answer would regualary call me 'Garry' (not my name). Phone calls only lasting 30 seconds as he was ' busy'. Two week passed with Tom not returning phone calls, tried the other number who said just text Tom, we tried that and he replied once. No further contact from him. Last week, after 3 months of this, a guy called Kim from dollar solar called out of the blue to say installation is 'next week' and that they are paying way more to the contractors that they normally would ( as if it was our fault ). We had lost faith in this company and their reliability by this stage and chose to cancel. The price is too good to be true. Their lack of communication is a true sign of how dangerous it would be to go with a company like this. I am sure if a problem occurred , they would just use their technique of avoiding your phone calls that Tom does so well. They say they provide solar across Australia, we are 3 hours from canberra. If you are regional or remote I would also avoid this company as they will drag you along for month, giving you false hope.",
